# Outside loops a store into a list has one arm in line, for the kind of storage that it expects: the storage of values. A list that has only ever held small integers has the storage of int32, so every such store
# left for the stub. An int32 is stored as the same boxed word in both kinds, so the one arm admits both: the storage of values is asked first, as before, the storage of int32 behind it.
# REQUIRES: as-written
# RUN: compile Int32StoresSharingBoxedPath mechanisms=all
# CHECK: statistic Int32StoresSharingBoxedPath 1
